{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T18:34:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-01T00:04:30+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-01T00:04:39+05:30\nThe search for \"site:apple.com/in macbook-air M5 15 inch specifications price\" returned the following summary:\nThe 15-inch MacBook Air with the M5 chip is a current model available in India. Below are the key specifications and pricing details.\n\n### **Specifications (15-inch MacBook Air, M5 Chip)**\n*   **Chip:** Apple M5 chip\n    *   10-core CPU (4 performance cores and 6 efficiency cores)\n    *   10-core GPU with hardware-accelerated ray tracing\n    *   16-core Neural Engine\n    *   153GB/s memory bandwidth\n*   **Display:** 15.3-inch (diagonal) Liquid Retina display with LED-backlit IPS technology; 2880x1864 native resolution at 224 pixels per inch, 500 nits brightness, and support for 1 billion colours (P3 wide colour, True Tone).\n*   **Memory:** Starts at 16GB unified memory (configurable to 24GB or 32GB).\n*   **Storage:** Starts at 512GB SSD (configurable to 1TB, 2TB, or 4TB).\n*   **Battery & Power:** Up to 18 hours of video playback; supports charging via MagSafe 3 or Thunderbolt/USB-C ports.\n*   **Ports:** \n    *   MagSafe 3 charging port\n    *   3.5mm headphone jack\n    *   Two Thunderbolt 4 (USB-C) ports (supports Charging, DisplayPort, Thunderbolt 4, and USB 4)\n*   **Connectivity:** Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6.\n*   **External Display Support:** Supports up to two external displays (e.g., two 6K displays at 60Hz or one 8K display).\n\n### **Price in India**\n*   **Starting Price:** The 15-inch MacBook Air with M5 starts at **₹1,79,900 (MRP)**.\n*   **Education Pricing:** Educational savings are available for eligible students and staff, which can reduce the starting price to approximately **₹1,67,900**.\n\n*Note: Pricing and availability may vary based on ongoing promotions, retail offers, or specific configuration choices (RAM/Storage upgrades). You can verify the latest offers and purchase directly through the [official Apple India website](https://www.apple.com/in).*"}
{"step_index":69,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T18:34:39Z","content":"Priyanshu, good news — you have the **better one**.\n\nYour config:\n- **MacBook Air M5 15-inch, 16GB, 512GB, Midnight, ₹1,79,900**\n\nThis is the **base model of the 15-inch Air**, and here's the key thing — **the 15-inch Air comes with the 10-core GPU as standard**. It's not the 8-core.\n\n| What you have | Spec |\n|:---|:---|\n| **CPU** | 10-core (4 Super Cores + 6 Efficiency) |\n| **GPU** | **10-core** ✅ (not the 8-core) |\n| **Neural Accelerators** | **10** (one per GPU core) |\n| **Neural Engine** | 16-core NPU |\n| **RAM** | 16 GB |\n| **Storage** | 512 GB |\n| **Memory Bandwidth** | 153 GB/s |\n| **Wi-Fi** | Wi-Fi 7 |\n\nThe 8-core GPU is only on the base **13-inch** Air (which starts at ₹1,24,900 in India). The **15-inch always ships with the full 10-core GPU**. So you're getting all 10 Neural Accelerators — the same GPU silicon as the base M5 MacBook Pro.\n\nYou don't need to upgrade anything GPU-wise. You already have the top base M5 config.\n\n**The only thing worth considering** — and I said this in the previous report — is whether 16GB RAM is enough for your use case. If you're doing normal work (coding, browsing, office, media), 16GB is fine. If you plan to run local AI models or you're a heavy multitasker (20+ Chrome tabs + Docker + IDE simultaneously), the jump to 24GB would cost more but would extend the machine's useful life by 1-2 years."}
